/* Isolation probe: an extra predicate argument that is PASSED THROUGH unchanged.
   Answers in well under a second, because the muCLP optimizer's constant-argument
   erasure sees that `d` is 0 at every call site and removes it, so the
   well-founded template is built over two coordinates and is identical to the
   version with no third argument at all.  Its twin `..._deadarg_alt_valid.hes`
   differs only in that `d` alternates, and takes about 85 times as long.
   Both are valid, and `d` is never read in either. */
Main 0
s.t.
Main (z:int): bool =mu forall (a:int). forall (b:int). (a = 0 /\ b = 0) \/ Q a b 0;
Q (a:int) (b:int) (d:int): bool =mu a > 0 /\ b >= 0 \/ Q (-b) a d;
